k of a crash.","remedy":"Toyota will notify owners, and dealers will replace the fuel pump assembly with an improved one, free of charge.  Owners of specific models were notified that remedy parts were available starting January 21, 2021.  Owners of other models will be notified as remedy parts become available.  Remedy parts should be available for all affected vehicles by late March 2021.  Owners may contact Toyota customer service at 1-888-270-9371 or Lexus customer service at 1-800-255-3987.  Note: This recall is an expansion of recall 20V-012.  Toyota's number for this recall is 20TA02.  Lexus' number for this recall is 20LA01.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":1525742,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=20V682000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":65,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2020","make":"TOYOTA","model":"SIENNA"},{"year":"2017","make":"LEXUS","model":"RX350"},{"year":"2019","make":"LEXUS","model":"GS300"},{"year":"2019","make":"LEXUS","model":"GS 350"},{"year":"2019","make":"LEXUS","model":"IS 350"},{"year":"2019","make":"LEXUS","model":"RX350"},{"year":"2019","make":"LEXUS","model":"RC 300"},{"year":"2019","make":"LEXUS","model":"RC 350"},{"year":"2019","make":"LEXUS","model":"IS 300"},{"year":"2019","make":"LEXUS","model":"LS500"},{"year":"2019","make":"LEXUS","model":"ES350"},{"year":"2019","make":"LEXUS","model":"LX570"},{"year":"2018","make":"LEXUS","model":"NX300"},{"year":"2019","make":"LEXUS","model":"NX300"},{"year":"2019","make":"LEXUS","model":"GX460"},{"year":"2018","make":"TOYOTA","model":"HIGHLANDER"},{"year":"2018","make":"TOYOTA","model":"SIENNA"},{"year":"2018","make":"TOYOTA","model":"TACOMA"},{"year":"2018","make":"LEXUS","model":"GS 350"},{"year":"2019","make":"TOYOTA","model":"AVALON"},{"year":"2019","make":"TOYOTA","model":"4RUNNER"},{"year":"2019","make":"TOYOTA","model":"CAMRY"},{"year":"2019","make":"TOYOTA","model":"HIGHLANDER"},{"year":"2019","make":"TOYOTA","model":"LAND CRUISER"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":true},{"campaign":"19V877000","received":"2019-12-11","manufacturer":"Toyota Motor Engineering & Manufacturing","component":"SEAT BELTS: REAR/OTHER:BUCKLE ASSEMBLY","summary":"Toyota Motor Engineering & Manufacturing (Toyota) is recalling certain 2019-2020 C-HR and 2020 Corolla and Corolla Hybrid vehicles equipped with rear seat belt assemblies with a dual-mode locking mechanism.  The seat belt webbing sensor locking mechanism may not lock as intended.","consequence":"In the event of a crash involving multiple impacts, the seat belt may not properly restrain the occupant, increasing the risk of injury.","remedy":"Toyota will notify owners, and dealers will inspect the rear seat belt assembly production dates, and replace the assemblies, as necessary, free of charge.  The recall began February 7, 2020.  Owners may contact Toyota customer service at 1-888-270-9371.  Toyota's numbers for this recall are 19TB22 and 19TA22.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":9468,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=19V877000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":4,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2019","make":"TOYOTA","model":"C-HR"},{"year":"2020","make":"TOYOTA","model":"COROLLA"},{"year":"2020","make":"TOYOTA","model":"C-HR"},{"year":"2020","make":"TOYOTA","model":"COROLLA HYBRID"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"23V865000","received":"2023-12-20","manufacturer":"Toyota Motor Engineering & Manufacturing","component":"AIR BAGS:SENSOR:OCCUPANT CLASSIFICATION","summary":"Toyota Motor Engineering & Manufacturing (Toyota) is recalling certain 2020-2021 Avalon, Avalon Hybrid, Corolla, Highlander, Highlander Hybrid, RAV4, RAV4 Hybrid, Lexus ES350, Lexus RX350, Lexus RX450H, 2021 Sienna Hybrid, Lexus ES250, 2020-2022 Camry, Camry Hybrid, and ES300H vehicles.  A short circuit may develop in the Occupant Classification System (OCS) sensor, preventing the front passenger air bag from deploying.","consequence":"An air bag that does not deploy during a crash increases the risk of injury.","remedy":"Dealers will inspect and replace the sensor as necessary, free of charge.  Interim letters notifying owners of the safety risk were mailed in February 2024. Some final remedy owner letters were mailed October 31, 2024. Letters will continue to be mailed in phases through January 2026. Owners may contact Toyota customer service at 1-800-331-4331.  Toyota's number for this recall is 23TB15/23TA15 Lexus 23LB03/23LA03.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":999901,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=23V865000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":30,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2021","make":"LEXUS","model":"RX HYBRID"},{"year":"2022","make":"LEXUS","model":"ES HYBRID"},{"year":"2020","make":"TOYOTA","model":"CAMRY"},{"year":"2021","make":"LEXUS","model":"ES HYBRID"},{"year":"2021","make":"TOYOTA","model":"RAV4"},{"year":"2021","make":"TOYOTA","model":"HIGHLANDER HYBRID"},{"year":"2020","make":"LEXUS","model":"ES HYBRID"},{"year":"2021","make":"LEXUS","model":"ES"},{"year":"2022","make":"TOYOTA","model":"CAMRY"},{"year":"2020","make":"TOYOTA","model":"AVALON"},{"year":"2020","make":"TOYOTA","model":"RAV4"},{"year":"2020","make":"TOYOTA","model":"HIGHLANDER"},{"year":"2020","make":"TOYOTA","model":"CAMRY HYBRID"},{"year":"2022","make":"TOYOTA","model":"CAMRY HYBRID"},{"year":"2021","make":"TOYOTA","model":"COROLLA"},{"year":"2021","make":"TOYOTA","model":"RAV4 HYBRID"},{"year":"2020","make":"LEXUS","model":"ES"},{"year":"2021","make":"TOYOTA